            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Late Career and \"Hedda Gabler\"</strong><br>\nIn his later career, Ibsen wrote \"Hedda Gabler,\" a play that examines the struggles of a woman trapped by societal conventions, which became one of his most famous and frequently performed plays.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Recognition</strong><br>\nIbsen's influence expanded beyond Norway, and he is often referred to as the \"father of modern drama.\" His works continue to be performed worldwide, demonstrating their timeless quality and relevance.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nHenrik Ibsen passed away on May 23, 1906, but left behind a legacy as one of the most important playwrights of his time. His works continue to provoke debate and inspire interpretations in theatre and literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
